From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa: sm6375: vote the three NoC paths, including IMEM

ipa_data_v4_11_sm6375 was given interconnect_count = 0 by patch 0025, on the
reasoning that mainline has no SM6375 interconnect provider and that the RPM
holds bimc/cnoc/snoc at INT_MAX anyway. That got the IPA to probe, and it was
verified that far and no further: the modem never reached a network at the
time, so the IPA never actually moved anything.

It does now, and the SoC watchdog-resets a few minutes after the modem
registers. The bisection is in HANDOFF-SESSION4.md session 14: ipa.ko loaded
with the modem registered dies in 3-10 minutes, either one alone runs
indefinitely, and with the radio on but *not* registered it survives 13+
minutes — that is, it needs the modem to actually attach, which is when the
modem installs its filter and route tables in IMEM.

The IPA reaches into IMEM here. That is not inference: before patch 0042 the
SMMU caught the access at iova=0x0c123080 from cbfrsynra=0x4a0, the IPA AP
context bank. And mainline only ever *maps* that window (ipa_imem_init); it
never tells the modem about it, so the modem firmware already knows the tables
live there and the AP's only job is to make the path work.

Nothing votes for that path. The vendor asks for three:

	blair.dtsi:3196, qcom,ipa@0x5800000
		interconnects = <&system_noc MASTER_IPA &bimc SLAVE_EBI>,
				<&system_noc MASTER_IPA &system_noc SLAVE_OCIMEM>,
				<&bimc MASTER_AMPSS_M0 &config_noc SLAVE_IPA_CFG>;
		interconnect-names = "ipa_to_ebi1", "ipa_to_imem", "appss_to_ipa";

while ipa_data-v4.11.c, which SM6375 borrows from qcm2290/sm6115, declares only
"memory" and "config". sdm845 (ipa_data-v3.5.1.c) declares "imem" too, so the
driver supports the path; this IPA version's data simply never needed it.

An on-chip SRAM slave with no voted path to it, touched by a DMA master, on a
SoC that resets without printing a character when a slave does not answer, is
a good enough explanation to test.

Bandwidths: "memory" and "config" keep the values the other v4.11 SoCs use.
"imem" takes sdm845's 350 MBps peak, which is the only figure mainline offers
for this path; the vendor expresses the same thing as bus vectors per
performance level rather than as a single number, and its NOMINAL row is of the
same order.

Needs the SM6375 interconnect provider (patch 0027) and the DT wiring
(patches 0028 and 0045).

--- a/drivers/net/ipa/data/ipa_data-v4.11.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/data/ipa_data-v4.11.c
@@ -416,6 +416,36 @@
 	.interconnect_count	= 0,
 };
 
+/* Interconnect rates for SM6375, which unlike the other IPA v4.11 SoCs needs a
+ * path to IMEM: the modem's filter and route tables live there and the IPA
+ * reads them through its own context bank. See blair.dtsi, ipa node,
+ * interconnect-names = "ipa_to_ebi1", "ipa_to_imem", "appss_to_ipa".
+ */
+static const struct ipa_interconnect_data ipa_interconnect_data_sm6375[] = {
+	{
+		.name			= "memory",
+		.peak_bandwidth		= 600000,	/* 600 MBps */
+		.average_bandwidth	= 150000,	/* 150 MBps */
+	},
+	/* Average rate is unused for the next two interconnects */
+	{
+		.name			= "imem",
+		.peak_bandwidth		= 350000,	/* 350 MBps */
+		.average_bandwidth	= 0,		/* unused */
+	},
+	{
+		.name			= "config",
+		.peak_bandwidth		= 74000,	/* 74 MBps */
+		.average_bandwidth	= 0,		/* unused */
+	},
+};
+
+static const struct ipa_power_data ipa_power_data_sm6375 = {
+	.core_clock_rate	= 60 * 1000 * 1000,	/* Hz */
+	.interconnect_count	= ARRAY_SIZE(ipa_interconnect_data_sm6375),
+	.interconnect_data	= ipa_interconnect_data_sm6375,
+};
+
 /* Configuration data for an SoC having IPA v4.11 */
 const struct ipa_data ipa_data_v4_11 = {
 	.version		= IPA_VERSION_4_11,
@@ -439,5 +469,5 @@
 	.endpoint_data		= ipa_gsi_endpoint_data,
 	.resource_data		= &ipa_resource_data,
 	.mem_data		= &ipa_mem_data_sm6375,
-	.power_data		= &ipa_power_data_no_icc,
+	.power_data		= &ipa_power_data_sm6375,
 };
